config MI_IORAPD_DUMMY
	tristate "Dummy /dev/iorap_dev node for Xiaomi launch boost"
	default y
	help
	  The vendor ROM ships /system_ext/bin/iorapd (launch boost preread) and
	  starts it from init.launch_boost.rc.  The first thing it does is

	      open("/dev/iorap_dev", O_RDWR)

	  and it exits right away when that open fails, so on a kernel without
	  the vendor driver init restarts it every five seconds forever:

	      E iorapd  : Cannot open /dev/iorap_dev, errno=2

	  iorapd treats every ioctl as optional, though: LB_GET_VERSION failing
	  makes it fall back to its v2 preread implementation, and
	  LB_GET_PREREAD_INFO failing makes it skip the preread for that launch.

	  This driver provides a node that always opens and reports a preread
	  engine that supports nothing, which is enough to keep iorapd alive.
	  It does not implement prereading: no file ranges are ever handed back.

	  Say Y unless you turn launch boost off with
	  persist.sys.stability.PrereadEnable=false.
